Sure! Here is a simple **HTML profile page** with the profile names **Yoga** and **Baba**:

```
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Profiles - Yoga & Baba</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f2f2f2;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 40px;
            text-align: center;
        }

        h1 {
            color: #333;
        }

        .profiles {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            gap: 30px;
            margin-top: 30px;
        }

        .profile {
            background-color: white;
            width: 250px;
            padding: 25px;
            border-radius: 15px;
            box-shadow: 0 5px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
        }

        .profile img {
            width: 120px;
            height: 120px;
            border-radius: 50%;
            object-fit: cover;
        }

        .profile h2 {
            color: #4CAF50;
        }

        .profile p {
            color: #666;
        }

        .profile button {
            background-color: #4CAF50;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            cursor: pointer;
        }

        .profile button:hover {
            background-color: #388E3C;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <h1>My Profiles</h1>

    <div class="profiles">

        <!-- Yoga Profile -->
        <div class="profile">
            <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/120" alt="Yoga Profile">
            <h2>Yoga</h2>
            <p>Yoga lover and fitness enthusiast.</p>
            <button>View Profile</button>
        </div>

        <!-- Baba Profile -->
        <div class="profile">
            <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/120" alt="Baba Profile">
            <h2>Baba</h2>
            <p>Peaceful, positive and spiritual person.</p>
            <button>View Profile</button>
        </div>

    </div>

</body>
</html>
```

Save it as **`profile.html`** and open it in your browser.
